description:
Objective: CQ-I06 DoD 2. A packaged plugin must contain every production helper asset it needs, and no test artifacts. Three defects were verified on 2026-10-30:
(a) packages/moe-proxy/tsconfig.json compiles src/*.test.ts. Its dist/ therefore holds index.test.js, input-framing.test.js, utils.test.js and workerType.test.js, with their .d.ts and .map files. Both bundlers copy that dist wholesale: moe-jetbrains/build.gradle.kts through from(bundledProxyDir), and moe-vscode/scripts/bundle-assets.mjs.
(b) The daemon build compiles the test-only src/tools/toolTestHarness.ts into dist/tools/toolTestHarness.js, and both plugins ship it. Only *.test.ts files import it.
(c) Both IDEs' Managed VM panels (CQ-I03, CQ-I05) spawn scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs. It ships only because the bundlers copy local-runner/**: no bundler required-list, onboarding check or bundle test names it.

Deliverable:
- packages/moe-daemon/tsconfig.json excludes src/tools/toolTestHarness.ts.
- Both bundlers add vm-control.mjs to their required local-runner assets, and drop **/*.test.* and **/*.spec.* from the daemon and proxy dist copies.
- scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs, in its packaged-bundle block, does three things:
  - requires local-runner/vm-control.mjs;
  - runs the packaged vm-control.mjs with no arguments and asserts exit 2 and exactly {"code":"VM_CONTROL_INPUT_INVALID"}. That proves its whole static import closure loads from the bundle, without touching Multipass, the ledger or the daemon;
  - fails on any test artifact under the bundle's daemon/, proxy/ or scripts/, excluding node_modules.
- scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs covers all of it.

Out of scope:
- the proxy tsconfig, which keeps typechecking proxy tests at build;
- what the npm-published moe-proxy package contains;
- node_modules dev dependencies;
- ci.yml and docs, which belong to CQ-I06;
- any runtime behaviour change.

Verification (run fresh, exit 0 required): node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs
